course: dictionary
lesson: 11469
title: Advertised: told, shown, and promised
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To advertise something means to tell lots of people about it so they will buy it or go to it. When it is past tense, «The shop advertised a new bike in the window», it means the shop told people about the bike. Look at the words around it: a shop, a window, a bike. Those clues tell you what happened.
explain: Advertised can also be an adjective. It describes something shown in an advert. «The advertised price was 40 pounds» means the price shown in the advert. Clues help again: price tells you it is about money, and advert tells you where the price was shown.
explain: «The kettle works as advertised.» This means the kettle does what the advert promised. Works is the clue: it works the way the advert said it would. Always check by swapping in your meaning. Does «the kettle works as the advert promised» still make sense? Yes, so you have it right.
fact: Advertise means to tell the public about something so they will buy it or come to it.
fact: Advertised is the past form of advertise, and it can also be an adjective.
fact: «The advertised price» means the price shown in an advert, before any discount or extra.
fact: «As advertised» means exactly as the advert promised.
fact: A good check is to swap in "shown in an advert" or "told people about" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The shop advertised a new bike in its window.» What does advertised mean here? | Broke it into pieces | Gave it away for free to the first child | Hid it from everyone | *Told people about it so they would want to buy it
exercise: «The advertised price was 40 pounds, but the shop took 10 pounds off.» What is the advertised price? | *40 pounds, the price shown in the advert | 10 pounds, the amount taken off | Free | 30 pounds, the price after the discount
exercise: «The new games console works as advertised.» What does as advertised suggest? | It was sold in a shop called Advertised | It is very old and needs fixing | *It does what the advert promised | It is broken and cannot be used
test: What does advertise mean? | Wrap a present in paper | *Tell people about something so they will buy it | Ask the price of a bus ticket | Hide something in a box so no one sees it
test: «The tablet was advertised at 120 pounds, but it was sold for 90 pounds.» Which price is the advertised price? | Free | *120 pounds | 30 pounds | 90 pounds
exam: «The phone was advertised as waterproof, and it stayed dry in the pool.» Why did the phone work as advertised? | It was sold in a swimming pool | It was advertised on a bus | It was too expensive to buy | *It did what the advert promised, because it stayed dry
